    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96370.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "There's no doubt that it's going to be 10x where we are right now within the next decade. And so when you say, and again, you look at the recommendations that are coming down the pike this March of 2020, some of the responsibilities in the private sector when there's material breaches. summer responsibilities that are going to be placed upon C-suite executives and boards. Some of the recommendations on pen testing, penetration testing to make sure that our companies are resilient on the cyber tax that have come and will continue to come throughout the next decade. We need to be very cognizant that there is a fifth domain and not just in warfare, but In warfare, we talk about the first four domains are air, sea, space, and land. The fifth domain is cyber, and that fifth domain isn't just in the battlefield, but it's here, as I mentioned earlier, in that invisible war, on our smartphones, on our desktops, and on our servers here in the United States of America.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
